  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Site location Plan, 10041-101, 102, 103 and 106 received 03/03/2011,10041- 104 A, 107 C, 112 D and 114 C.19/04/2011 and 10041-105 C, 111 E and 115 G received 27/05/2011)  therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive  noise created by the ground floor use shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 5 - \"Before the development hereby permitted commences the applicant must either:\r\na.\tInvestigate the site for landfill gas to the satisfaction of the LPA, to ascertain whether gas protection measures are required.  Where measures are required the details shall be submitted to, and approved by, the LPA.\r\nOr;\r\nb.\tThe applicant shall install gas protection measures as a precautionary measure without first investigating the site.  The details of these measures shall be submitted to, and approved by, the LPA.\r\nc.\tFor a. and b. all required measures shall be installed before the development is first occupied.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - The parking spaces shown on drawing 10041-111 rev D shall be made available before the occupation of the first floor flats and shall be made permanently available thereafter for occupiers of the first floor flats unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - The amenity space together with the boundary fencing and bin stores shall be made available prior to the occupation of the first floor flats and shall be made permanently available thereafter for occupiers of the first floor flats unless otherwise agreed in writing beforehand with the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - The use shall not commence until the secure storage area within the site within the rear service area for the ground floor unit as shown on the approved plans with not less than two 1100 litre galvanised steel Eurobins has been made available, together with facilities for the separation and safe storage of glass, metal, plastics, cardboard, food waste and other recyclable materials which shall then be collected and taken to a suitable facility for recycling.  The storage area and bins shall be made permanently available before the use is commenced and no waste shall be stored outside the site or other than in the designated area.  The lids of the Eurobins shall be fixed shut at all times other than when waste is being emptied into them.  Non-recyclable and perishable waste shall be removed from site no less frequently than once a week.  Waste shall be removed as soon as the bins become full if this is earlier than the time of the normal weekly collection, unless additional covered and enclosed bins (as described above) have been provided and are thereafter made permanently available for the on-site storage of refuse and waste."
  ],
